\f0\fs26 \cf0 **1. Pawing/Rubbing Nose**\
He often rubs or pats his nose like a koala snuffling for scent or comfort\'97especially when thinking or fake-laughing.\
\
**2. Head Tilts**\
He cocks his head to one side, small eyes blinking slowly, as if considering a tricky eucalyptus leaf.\
\
**3. Ear Twitch/Scratch**\
When nervous or annoyed, his hand sneaks up to tug or scratch behind one hairy ear, much too gently for a grown man.\
\
**4. Cheek-Puffing**\
He sometimes puffs out his rounded cheeks when about to retort or absorb criticism, like a plush animal trying to look intimidating.\
\
**5. Slow Blinks**\
He has a tendency to stare with unblinking, half-lidded koala eyes at guests or cameras\'97a trick that comes off as either endearingly vacant or faintly menacing.\
\
**6. Gripping/Hugging Things**\
He unconsciously grips, hugs, or clings to objects with both hands\'97water bottles, lecterns, the arms of his chair\'97evoking a koala\'92s death grip on a tree branch.\
\
**7. Languid Shoulder Hunch**\
When listening, he hunches his broad shoulders, making himself appear simultaneously stocky and relaxed, just like a koala wedged in a forked branch.\
\
**8. Eucalyptus Habit (Joke/Reference)**\
He has a taste for strong, minty chewing gum, which people joke is just his way of always having \'93eucalyptus\'94 handy.\
\
**9. Sleepy Look**\
During long takes or boring meetings, his blink rate drops and his face takes on a dozy expression, as if perched up a tree about to nap for twelve hours.\
\
**10. Sudden, Clingy Hugs**\
He sometimes startles colleagues by giving unexpectedly affectionate, overlong hugs\'97media spin: \'93Australia\'92s favourite cuddler.\'94 Office reality: weird and memorable.\
